# Development Server Management

## Background Server with Hot Reload

Always run the development server in background mode with hot reload enabled:

```bash
# Start development server in background
cd apps/web; bun run dev
```

## Server Management Commands

### Start Server
```bash
# From project root
cd apps/web; bun run dev
```

### Stop Server
```bash
# Stop all Node.js and Bun processes
Get-Process | Where-Object {$_.ProcessName -like "*node*" -or $_.ProcessName -like "*bun*"} | Stop-Process -Force
```

### Clear Cache
```bash
# Clear Next.js cache
Remove-Item apps/web/.next -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Remove-Item apps/web/node_modules/.cache -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
```

### Check Server Status
```bash
# Check if server is running
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri http://localhost:3000/ -UseBasicParsing | Select-Object StatusCode, StatusDescription
```

## Important Notes

- Server runs on `http://localhost:3000` by default
- Hot reload is enabled automatically with `bun run dev`
- Always clear cache when encountering ENOENT errors
- Use PowerShell commands for Windows environment
- Background processes persist between terminal sessions

## Troubleshooting

If server fails to start:
1. Stop all existing processes
2. Clear Next.js cache
3. Restart server in background mode
4. Wait 10-15 seconds for full startup
5. Check server status with HTTP request
